            "claim_id": "c2",
            "status": "introduced",
            "necessary": "yes",
            "before": {
              "requirement": "Establish ProcGlobal before InitProcess; the old BaseInit route calls InitCommunication for shared memory and semaphore setup.",
              "applicability": "required",
              "harness_status": "sat",
              "reason": "The unchanged harness calls BaseInit before InitProcess. Before the change, BaseInit's documented shared memory setup call occupied that position.",
              "source_evidence": [
                {
                  "evidence_id": "loc-a90b28c8aab99af14ed55938",
                  "quote": "\t/*\n\t * Attach to shared memory and semaphores, and initialize our\n\t * input/output/debugging file descriptors.\n\t */\n\tInitCommunication();\n\tDebugFileOpen();\n\n\t/* Do local initialization of file, storage and buffer managers */\n\tInitFileAccess();\n\tInitSync();\n\tsmgrinit();\n\tInitBufferPoolAccess();\n"
                },
                {
                  "evidence_id": "loc-1d87f345f565e433f5f439bd",
                  "quote": "\t * Set up process table\n\t */\n\tif (!IsUnderPostmaster)\n\t\tInitProcGlobal();\n\tCreateSharedProcArray();\n"
                },
                {
                  "evidence_id": "loc-d25de614e585a0f1a136c1d1",
                  "quote": "\t/*\n\t * ProcGlobal should be set up already (if we are a backend, we inherit\n\t * this by fork() or EXEC_BACKEND mechanism from the postmaster).\n\t */\n\tif (ProcGlobal == NULL)\n\t\telog(PANIC, \"proc header uninitialized\");\n"
                }
              ]
            },
            "after": {
              "requirement": "Establish ProcGlobal explicitly before InitProcess because BaseInit no longer performs shared memory setup.",
              "applicability": "required",
              "harness_status": "unsat",
              "reason": "The same harness calls BaseInit then InitProcess, with no shared memory setup between them. After the change, BaseInit no longer calls InitCommunication; InitProcess rejects NULL ProcGlobal.",
              "source_evidence": [
                {
                  "evidence_id": "loc-ceb5d535b728d2bf3538de70",
                  "quote": "void\nBaseInit(void)\n{\n\tAssert(MyProc != NULL);\n\n\t/*\n\t * Initialize our input/output/debugging file descriptors.\n\t */\n\tDebugFileOpen();\n\n\t/* Do local initialization of file, storage and buffer managers */\n\tInitFileAccess();\n\tInitSync();\n\tsmgrinit();\n\tInitBufferPoolAccess();\n}\n"
                },
                {
                  "evidence_id": "loc-e8e6ff466d6b96ce5d438532",
                  "quote": "\t/*\n\t * ProcGlobal should be set up already (if we are a backend, we inherit\n\t * this by fork() or EXEC_BACKEND mechanism from the postmaster).\n\t */\n\tif (ProcGlobal == NULL)\n\t\telog(PANIC, \"proc header uninitialized\");\n"
                },
                {
                  "evidence_id": "loc-7c846baea083b6365ea46cc7",
                  "quote": "\t * Set up process table\n\t */\n\tif (!IsUnderPostmaster)\n\t\tInitProcGlobal();\n\tCreateSharedProcArray();\n"
                }
              ]
            },
            "same_blocker": "no",
            "reason": "The harness sequence is fixed across both versions. Removing InitCommunication from BaseInit changes its ProcGlobal prerequisite from satisfied to unsatisfied. The new MyProc assertions may fail earlier in an assertion-enabled build, but they do not supply ProcGlobal.",
            "error": null,
            "missing_information": []
          }
